Registered as a scheduled task with -AtStartup (like Sentinel), or

Dropped into one of these auto-run locations:

C:\ProgramData\Microsoft\Windows\Start Menu\Programs\Startup

Registry HKCU:\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run

And because it has param([int]$AutoStart = 1) at the top, it always calls Run-All immediately and exits, so you never see a menu.

Why does the console pop open?
Even though you hide the three child processes with Start-Process -WindowStyle Hidden, the drift_launcher.ps1 itself is being launched in a visible PowerShell console by Task Scheduler (or Startup).

To fix this, we need one of these two solutions:

Option A – Keep it but make it invisible
